1 DISMOUNT
    The DISMOUNT command detaches the disk-image container currently
    mounted on a device, flushing any pending writes and closing the
    underlying container file.  The device itself remains known to the
    console; only its mounted volume is removed.  A later MOUNT command
    can attach a different container to the same device name.

    Dismounting a device with nothing currently mounted on it is an error,
    and so is dismounting one with files open (a process the console
    stopped may still have some): close them, or STOP the process,
    first.  When govax exits, every volume is dismounted regardless.

    Syntax:

        DISMOUNT <device>

    Parameter:

        <device>        The device name to detach, such as DUA0.  A
                        trailing colon is optional.  A logical name, such
                        as the DISK$label name MOUNT defined, is
                        translated first.

    Example:

        DISMOUNT DUA0

    See also the help for MOUNT and SHOW DEVICE.
